k Program Management [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety/the-importance-of-biosecurity-in-biorisk-program-management.html) **Cristine C. Lawson, Ph.D., RBP, CBSP ** BSAT Biorisk Program Office, Department of Defense November 19 Biorisk Management Performance Evaluation **Michael Pentella, PhD, D(ABMM)** State Hygienic Laboratory, University of Iowa December 17 Biorisk Management: Continuous Improvement **Patricia Olinger , JM** Varro Life SciencesBEAMS, LLC December 5, 2024 Sources Print Share [ Facebook ](https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov ""Share to Facebook"") [ LinkedIn ](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov&title=Living%20with%20High%20Blood%20Pressure ""Share to LinkedIn"") [ Twitter ](https://twitter.com/share?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov&text=Living%20with%20High%20Blood%20Pressure ""Share to Twitter"") [ Syndicate ](https://tools.cdc.gov/medialibrary/index.aspx#/sharecontent/https://https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety/index.html ""Embed this Page"") Content Source: [Division of Laboratory Systems](/laboratory-systems/php/about/index.html) Sources * [Division of Laboratory Systems (DLS)](/laboratory-systems/php/about)",,,,,,,基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=direct；quality_score=0.6835。,CDC ECHO Biosafety | https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety/index.html,网页,CDC ECHO Biosafety,CDC,,,https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety/index.html,2026-04-27,,draft,cdc;echo biosafety;capacity building,en
WEB82-021-001,CDC ECHO Biosafety 2023,培训,安全规范,biosafety,3,生物;综合安全,What practical biosafety lessons and implementation cases are included in CDC ECHO 2023,What practical biosafety lessons and implementation cases are included in CDC ECHO 2023有哪些要点？,"January 8, 2025 # Extension for Community Healthcare Outcomes (ECHO) Biosafety Program: 2023 ## What to know The ECHO Biosafety Program addresses challenges in clinical and public health laboratories through the development of a community of practice (CoP). This page contains the ECHO Biosafety session materials from 2023. ## Background Logos for CDC, University of New Mexico Health Sciences, and Project ECHO. This project is an adaptation of the clinician-based [ECHO Model](https://echo.unm.edu/)™, developed by the University of New Mexico Health Sciences Center. The [ECHO Model](https://echo.unm.edu/)™ invites peers to engage in a virtual environment on a frequent, regular basis where they share support, guidance, and feedback. The goal of this project is to use the ECHO Model to improve biosafety in clinical and public health laboratories by increasing the knowledge and skills of the biosafety CoP members to address previously identified biosafety gaps. The objectives of this project are to: * Discuss biosafety challenges among clinical and public health laboratory professionals * Foster collaborations and sharing of laboratory biosafety expertise * Promote the application of best biosafety practices and advance the culture and practice of laboratory safety The ECHO Biosafety sessions are 60-90 minutes each and occur every month. The CoP members convening at the sessions will share best practices, tools, and resources to address biosafety gaps in clinical and public health laboratories. For questions, contact [DLSbiosafety@cdc.gov](mailto:DLSbiosafety@cdc.gov). ### Resource Find archived content from the [ECHO sessions on diagnostic excellence](/lab-quality/php/echo/) piloted by the Division of Laboratory Systems (DLS) in 2020. ## 2023 ECHO Biosafety Sessions Month Area of Discussion Speakers January 31 Public Health Laboratory Professional Burnout and Effect on Safety [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/public-health-laboratory-professional-burnout-and-effect-on-safety.html) **Anthony Tran, DrPH, MPH, D(ABMM)** California Department of Public Health February 28 Risk Assessment in Clinical Laboratories [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/risk-assessment-clinical-laboratories.html) **Crystal Fortune , MPH, MLS (ASCP)CM RBP (ABSA)** Montana Laboratory Services Bureau March 22 Safely Implementing New Diagnostics Platforms Commonly Used in Clinical Laboratories [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/safely-implementing-new-diagnostics-platforms-commonly-used-clinical-laboratories.html) **Christina Egan, PhD** **Michael J. Perry, MS, MS Ed.** New York State Department of Health April 25 Decontamination of Laboratory Equipment [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/decontamination-laboratory-equipment.html) **Shawn G. Gibbs, PhD, MBA, CIH** School of Public Health, Texas A&M University **Aurora Le, PhD, MPH, CPH, CSP** School of Public Health, University of Michigan May 30 PPE Use (What, Who, Why, When, and How) [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/ppe-use.html) **Peter C. Iwen, PhD, D(ABMM), F(AAM)** Nebraska Public Health Laboratory University Nebraska Medical Center June 27 Laboratory Acquired Infections [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/laboratory-acquired-infections.html) **Sheldon Campbell, MD, PhD** **David Peaper, PhD** Yale University School of Medicine July 18 Biosafety Challenges in Alaska [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/biosafety-challenges-alaska.html) **John Laurance** Alaska State Public Health Laboratories August 29 Safety Challenges with Specimen Collection, Transport, Accessioning, and Storage [Session Materials](https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/safety-challenges-specimens.html) **Joey Stringer** **Kayle Cirrincione** Dallas County Health and Human Services September 26 Medical Waste Management [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/medical-waste-management.html) **Nikki Parrish, PhD** Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine October 31 Quality in Biosafety [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/quality-biosafety.html) **Jill J. Power, MS, M(ASCP), CMQ/OE(ASQ)** New Hampshire Public Health Laboratories November 28 Laboratory Professional Vaccine Compliance and Effect on Safety [Session Materials](/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/laboratory-professional-vaccine-compliance-effect-safety.html) **Michael Pentella, PhD, D(ABMM)** State Hygienic Laboratory,University of Iowa January 8, 2025 Sources Print Share [ Facebook ](https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov ""Share to Facebook"") [ LinkedIn ](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov&title=Living%20with%20High%20Blood%20Pressure ""Share to LinkedIn"") [ Twitter ](https://twitter.com/share?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov&text=Living%20with%20High%20Blood%20Pressure ""Share to Twitter"") [ Syndicate ](https://tools.cdc.gov/medialibrary/index.aspx#/sharecontent/https://https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/index.html ""Embed this Page"") Content Source: [Division of Laboratory Systems](/laboratory-systems/php/about/index.html)",,,,,,,基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=direct；quality_score=0.6815。,CDC ECHO Biosafety 2023 | https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/index.html,网页,CDC ECHO Biosafety 2023,CDC,,,https://www.cdc.gov/safe-labs/php/echo-biosafety-2023/index.html,2026-04-27,,draft,cdc;echo biosafety 2023;training,en
WEB82-022-001,CDC Laboratory Systems About,实验室管理,安全规范,general,3,综合安全;quality,How does CDC laboratory systems guidance support quality and safety governance,How does CDC laboratory systems guidance support quality and safety governance有哪些要点？,"# About Division of Laboratory Systems Nov. 21, 2024 ## Key points * The Division of Laboratory Systems (DLS) advances the quality and safety of clinical and public health laboratory testing and services nationwide. * Advancing laboratory systems improves public health and patient outcomes. ## Spotlight ### What's new in DLS [Celebrate Lab Week 2026: Laboratory Professionals Safeguard Health](/lab-week/php/about/index.html) [CLIA Personnel Qualifications and Responsibilities: High Complexity Testing eLearning Course Is Now on OneLab REACH™](https://reach.cdc.gov/course/clia-personnel-qualifications-and-responsibilities-high-complexity-testing) [OneLab™ Announces New OneLab VR Resources](https://reach.cdc.gov/onelabvr) [CDC's Basic Microscopy Resources Are Now on OneLab REACH™](https://reach.cdc.gov/course/basic-microscopy-microbiology-curriculum) [Laboratory Training Course: Adult Blood Culture Collection](https://reach.cdc.gov/course/adult-blood-culture-collection) [NGS Quality Initiative Releases Pathway to Quality-Focused Testing Tool](/lab-quality/php/pathway/pathway-to-testing.html) ## Who We Are Laboratory systems encompass the core technical domains that all clinical and environmental laboratories must maintain regardless of location, size, or expertise. These include quality and safety management systems, informatics and data systems, training and workforce development programs, active partnerships and outreach, and preparedness planning for responding to unusual circumstances or emergencies. Together, these systems enable the testing community to produce reliable laboratory results that advance patient care and protect public health. ### Vision ****Exemplary laboratory practice and systems strengthen clinical care, public health, and emergency response. ### Mission ****Improve public health and patient outcomes by advancing laboratory systems. ## Priorities ### Quality and safety The Division of Laboratory Systems (DLS) advances the quality and safety of clinical and public health laboratory testing and services nationwide. DLS fosters the development of laboratory standards and guidelines and supports regulatory programs. DLS works in partnership with the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) and the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) by providing scientific and technical expertise for the CLIA program. **Keep Reading** [About Quality and Safety Systems](/laboratory-systems/php/about/quality-safety-systems.html) ### Informatics and data science DLS enhances public health surveillance and response by strengthening the exchange of laboratory data between organizations and systems, and conducting analyses of large laboratory-based datasets. **Keep Reading** [About Informatics and Data Science](/laboratory-systems/php/about/informatics-data-science.html) ### Training and workforce development DLS works to improve the knowledge, competency, reliability, and sustainability of the clinical and public health laboratory workforce nationwide. Specifically, DLS supports the clinical and public health laboratory workforce through the development of training products and resources and implementation of competency guidelines for public health laboratory professionals. **Keep Reading** [About Training and Workforce Development](/laboratory-systems/php/about/training-workforce-development.html) Nov. 21, 2024 Sources Print Share [ Facebook ](https://www.facebook.com/ ""Share to Facebook"") [ LinkedIn ](https://www.linkedin.com/ ""Share to LinkedIn"") [ Twitter ](https://twitter.com/ ""Share to Twitter"") [ Syndicate ](https://tools.cdc.gov/medialibrary/index.aspx#/sharecontent ""Embed this Page"") Content Source: Sources * Graber ML, ""[The incidence of diagnostic error in medicine](https://qualitysafety.bmj.com/content/22/Suppl_2/ii21),"" _BMJ Qual Saf_ 2013;22:ii21-ii27. * Leape LL, Berwick DM, and Bates DW, ""[Counting Deaths Due to Medical Errors—Reply](https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/article-abstract/1845204?redirect=true),"" _JAMA_ 2002;288(19):2405. * Tehrani, AS Saber, et al., ""[25-year summary of US malpractice claims for diagnostic errors 1986-2000: an analysis from the National Practitioner Bank,](https://qualitysafety.bmj.com/content/22/8/672)"" _BMJ Qual Saf_ , 22, 672-680 (2013). * Winters B, et al. ""[Diagnostic errors in the intensive care unit: a systematic review of autopsy studies](https://qualitysafety.bmj.com/content/21/11/894?ijkey=6a806ceac40363143b11074998ab670d40d56b76&keytype2=tf_ipsecsha),"" _BMJ Qual Saf_ 2012;21:894–902.",,,,,,,基于公开网页资料自动抽取，导入知识库前请人工复核。提取通道=direct；quality_score=0.6727。,CDC Laboratory Systems About | https://www.cdc.gov/laboratory-systems/php/about/index.html,网页,CDC Laboratory Systems About,CDC,,,https://www.cdc.gov/laboratory-systems/php/about/index.html,2026-04-27,,draft,cdc;laboratory systems;quality,en
