WEB82-030-001,CCOHS Chemical Effects,化学,安全规范,chemical,3,化学;toxicology,How should chemical health effects information be used in laboratory risk assessment and controls,How should chemical health effects information be used in laboratory risk assessment and controls有哪些要点？,"# Effects on the body In order for a chemical to become hazardous to a person's health, it must first contact or enter the body and the chemical must have some biological effect on the body. Once chemicals are in the body, they are distributed by the blood stream and can attack and harm organs which are far away from the original point of entry as well as where they entered the body. Choose from the following available resources Health and Safety Fact Sheets (OSH Answers) Health and Safety Fact Sheets (OSH Answers) --- [How Do Particulates Enter the Respiratory System?](/oshanswers/chemicals/how_do.html) [How Workplace Chemicals Enter the Body](/oshanswers/chemicals/how_chem.html) [Synergism and related terms](/oshanswers/chemicals/synergism.html) [What are the Effects of Dust on the Lungs?](/oshanswers/chemicals/lungs_dust.html) [What is a LD50 and LC50?](/oshanswers/chemicals/ld50.html) [What Makes Chemicals Poisonous](/oshanswers/chemicals/poisonou.html) I want to... [See what's new](/oshanswers/whats_new.html) [Learn more about OSH Answers](/oshanswers/about.html) [ VIEW ALL FACT SHEETS ](/oshanswers/) Databases Databases For more information or to purchase access, click on the title Starting From | Starting From ---|--- [CHEMINFO](/products/cheminfo/)| **$300.00** [OSH References](/products/oshreferences/)| **$650.00** [RTECS® (Registry of Toxic Effects of Chemical Substances)](/products/rtecs/)| **$350.00** I want to... [Learn more about databases](/products/faqs.html#databases) [Request a demo](/products/ordering/request_demo.html) [ VIEW ALL DATABASES ](/products/databases/) Courses/e-Learning Courses/e-Learning For more information or to purchase access, click on the title Single Seat | Si